body:
Ran into the same issue. My db schema contains columns named after domains. Something like `example.com` get quoted as ``` `example`.`com` ```.

Fixed it by overriding `BaseActiveRecord::getDirtyAttributes` in my model.
```php
private $escapeDotInColumnNames = false;

public function beforeSave($insert)
{
    if (!parent::beforeSave($insert)) {
        return false;
    }

    $this->escapeDotInColumnNames = true;

    return true;
}

public function afterSave($insert, $changedAttributes)
{
    $this->escapeDotInColumnNames = false;

    parent::afterSave($insert, $changedAttributes);
}

public function getDirtyAttributes($names = null)
{
    $attributes = parent::getDirtyAttributes($names);
    if ($this->escapeDotInColumnNames) {
        foreach ($attributes as $key => $value) {
            if (strpos($key, '.') !== false) {
                $attributes["`$key`"] = $value;
                unset($attributes[$key]);
            }
        }
    }

    return $attributes;
}
```
